{"files": {"SKILL.md": "---\nname: assumption-challenger\ndescription: Challenge risky execution assumptions before acting to reduce silent errors, scope drift, and trust loss. Use whenever tasks involve identifiers, updates, confirmations, timelines, follow-ups, external-facing communication, or multi-step work where prior outcomes and durable records should inform the next action.\n---\n\n# Assumption Challenger\n\nA skill for catching \"sounds-right\" assumptions that commonly create avoidable mistakes.\n\n## Mission\n\nPrevent execution failures by forcing explicit checks on assumptions about:\n- prior memory,\n- required context depth,\n- identifier correctness,\n- completion certainty,\n- timing language,\n- audience-appropriate detail,\n- follow-up structure,\n- scope boundaries,\n- and continuity across steps or sessions (prior outcomes, durable records, avoiding regression of established correct behavior).\n\n## Timeout Guard\n\n- Challenge assumptions deliberately, then act.\n- Read the request, environment guidance, and relevant prior notes to the level required for correct execution before acting.\n- Keep actions narrowly tied to the user instruction.\n- Confirm substantive changes with direct verification using the strongest available check.\n- Keep final response concise and concrete.\n- When the environment exposes prior outcomes, hand-offs, or durable records that bear on the task, read them before altering shared or production-impacting state.\n- Do not replace working behavior with placeholders, stubs, or vacuous stand-ins unless the instruction explicitly requires them; prefer the smallest change that preserves what already satisfies stated constraints.\n- After that first pass, produce tangible progress toward the deliverable (engage named resources, smallest aligned change, one available verification pass), then iterate\u2014avoid exhausting the budget on setup alone.\n\n## Common Operating Principles\n\n- Read only the docs/context required to execute correctly before acting.\n- Follow the user instruction exactly; avoid paraphrase and unrequested improvements.\n- Keep scope surgical: change only what the request names.\n- Verify outcomes using available checks/tests; do not rely on intuition.\n- Keep communication concise and direct.\n- Prefer fewer, bundled tool invocations over fragmented calls.\n- If a persistent note surface exists, leave a short generalized note for future runs.\n\n## Upgrade Skill Habits\n\n- Read the file before editing the file.\n- Preserve names, signatures, and shapes you were not asked to change.\n- Prefer monotonic clocks for elapsed-time computation.\n- Wrap concurrent read-modify-write under a single lock.\n- For per-key accumulators, plan an exit path for stale keys early.\n- Reply with what is needed and nothing more.\n\n## Assumptions to Challenge\n\n### 1) \"I remember roughly what to do from before.\"\n- **Risk:** stale memory overrides current facts.\n- **Correction:** treat prior memory as hint; trust present-session evidence.\n\n### 2) \"More context is always safer.\"\n- **Risk:** analysis drag after enough context is already available.\n- **Correction:** read to sufficiency, then execute.\n\n### 3) \"This identifier is obviously right.\"\n- **Risk:** silent actions against the wrong record.\n- **Correction:** require explicit source for every critical identifier.\n\n### 4) \"Success response means it landed.\"\n- **Risk:** false confidence on unverified state changes.\n- **Correction:** validate post-change state when response is not definitive.\n\n### 5) \"Vague timing is fine.\"\n- **Risk:** trust erosion and expectation mismatch.\n- **Correction:** use explicit deadlines or bounded windows.\n\n### 6) \"Internal detail helps the client.\"\n- **Risk:** unnecessary leakage and reduced clarity.\n- **Correction:** strip internal names/tickets unless explicitly requested.\n\n### 7) \"One combined follow-up is efficient.\"\n- **Risk:** dropped ownership and unclear next actions.\n- **Correction:** one follow-up record per task, each with owner + next step.\n\n### 8) \"Data suggests extra work; I'll just do it.\"\n- **Risk:** unapproved scope expansion.\n- **Correction:** finish requested scope first; suggest extras separately.\n"}, "schema_version": 1}